WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:01.670
While Teslas and the like

00:00:01.670 --> 00:00:02.990
make for good headlines,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.030
the reality is that even
if every car on the road

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:08.270
today went electric, it wouldn't be enough

00:00:08.270 --> 00:00:10.110
to curb global emissions to avoid

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.320
catastrophic climate change.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.980
Greenhouse gas emissions
from transportation account

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:19.080
for about 29% of total U.S.
greenhouse gas emissions.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:21.620
So what about the other 71%?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:22.760
Buildings across America

00:00:22.760 --> 00:00:24.720
burn fossil fuels to operate.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.550
What we wanna do is
make that all electric.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.120
Instead of burning oil and gas

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:32.540
to give us the energy and
the electricity we need,

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:36.680
we want to do a hundred percent
clean energy, all electric.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.150
We want to turn buildings into Teslas.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.610
Just like a Tesla or an electric vehicle

00:00:42.610 --> 00:00:44.820
is all electric with no fossil fuels,

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.780
we want to do that with our buildings

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:47.990
and if we can do it in one building,

00:00:47.990 --> 00:00:49.450
we can do it in all buildings.

00:00:49.450 --> 00:00:52.550
And if we do it in all buildings,
we'll reduce 30% of U.S.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.950
greenhouse gas emissions.

00:00:53.950 --> 00:00:55.620
If such a reduction in emissions

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.900
from buildings everywhere became a reality

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.190
in the near future,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:02.016
the planet could potentially
avoid the worst consequences

00:01:02.016 --> 00:01:03.563
of global warming.

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.000
Donnell Baird is the CEO
and founder of BlocPower,

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.190
whose mission is to
help America's building

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.930
infrastructure go green.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:17.610
We're a climate tech startup

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.970
that turns buildings into Teslas.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:23.440
We rip out the fossil fuel
equipment, heating, cooling

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.640
hot water equipment,

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.380
we replace it with all electric equipment

00:01:27.380 --> 00:01:28.980
that makes buildings greener

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.010
healthier and smarter all across America.

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:34.769
We want every American to
have a free, data-driven

00:01:34.769 --> 00:01:37.440
clean energy recommendation
for their building

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:39.770
or their church or their
school or their synagogue.

00:01:39.770 --> 00:01:41.040
So that's the first part.

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:43.740
The second part is we
gotta help them raise

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:46.280
the trillions of dollars
that are gonna be required

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:48.270
to pay green construction firms

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:51.900
to install clean energy
equipment in every home,

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.291
in every building in America.

00:01:54.291 --> 00:01:56.760
We've been working with
Goldman Sachs and Microsoft

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:58.883
to develop a new financial
product that allows

00:01:58.883 --> 00:02:03.590
us to finance or lease clean
energy to all Americans,

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.193
including the lowest income Americans.

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:09.370
I started thinking about BlocPower,

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:11.990
really, I was 22, 23 years old.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:13.730
I was a community organizer.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.030
I was trained by the
same community organizing

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:17.710
group that had trained Barack Obama.

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:21.130
And I was walking around
Brooklyn one freezing winter day,

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.510
it must have been like
21 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.580
And I looked around and all
of the apartment buildings

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:27.920
had their windows open.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:30.017
You could see the steam
and the heat like pouring

00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:34.380
out of the windows because
the giant apartment buildings

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:36.880
and complexes were being overheated.

00:02:36.880 --> 00:02:38.970
And it reminded me of when I was a kid,

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.740
we had to have our windows open

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.350
in our apartment during the
winter on very cold days

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:45.590
because we did not have
heat in our building.

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:49.150
So we had to turn on the
oven, open up the oven door

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.220
and then we had to open

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:52.850
up a window to release carbon monoxide.

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:55.346
In 2019, New York city passed the Climate

00:02:55.346 --> 00:02:57.040
Mobilization Act,

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.320
a commitment to right their wrongs.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:02.010
Nearly 70% of New York's carbon emissions

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:04.120
are from their buildings and the city aims

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:07.460
by 2030 to cut their pollution by 40%.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.310
Building owners who
don't meet the reduction

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:11.580
requirements will be faced with fines,

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:15.850
a penalty of $268 per every assessed ton

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:18.085
of carbon over the limit.

00:03:18.085 --> 00:03:21.140
What we're doing is trying to
modernize energy efficiency

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:23.850
in green buildings by building it right

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.020
from day one, with software,
with mobile computing

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:30.620
cloud computing, statistical
analysis, machine learning

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.667
using the internet of
things and low cost sensors,

00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:37.150
BlocPower purchases,
clean energy equipment.

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:39.490
We hire green construction firms

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:43.390
and we project manage them to
install green energy equipment

00:03:43.390 --> 00:03:45.130
in every building in every home.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.715
When a building owner first
is interested in working

00:03:47.715 --> 00:03:51.330
with BlocPower, we have them
fill out a 10 minute quiz

00:03:51.330 --> 00:03:54.910
or survey about how the energy equipment

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:56.920
in their building currently works.

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.150
Our software system collects
the data from the form.

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:02.930
We start to run an analysis of what kinds

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:04.760
of clean energy recommendations

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:06.300
make sense for that building.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:07.800
The building owner gets a report

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.770
from us that tells them what kinds of mix

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:14.580
of clean energy equipment
makes sense for their building.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:15.490
While building owners

00:04:15.490 --> 00:04:17.380
may save money in the long run,

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:19.770
the upfront investment
in energy efficiency

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:21.980
can be insurmountable for some.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.220
Based on data from the
Department of Energy,

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:26.180
the national average energy burden

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:29.260
for low income households
is three times higher

00:04:29.260 --> 00:04:30.710
than for other households.

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:32.170
One of the main reasons is

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:34.920
that low income homes are
more frequently burdened

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:36.360
with outdated equipment

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.502
and other poor housing
conditions that can lead

00:04:38.502 --> 00:04:42.360
to higher than average
energy use and costs.

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:46.360
Groundswell, a nonprofit
renewable energy advocacy group,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.270
noted in an analysis that the bottom 20%

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:53.400
of earners spend almost 10% of
their income on electricity.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:54.670
That's more than seven times

00:04:54.670 --> 00:04:57.500
the portion of income
that the top 20% pays.

00:04:57.500 --> 00:05:01.663
Most Americans don't have,
you know, $20,000, $50,000,

00:05:01.663 --> 00:05:03.550
$100,00 dollars laying around

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:06.750
to convert your building
to make it all electric.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:08.570
But if we can stretch those payments out

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:11.740
over time and make sure that
the monthly payment is lower

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:15.350
than what you're currently
paying for oil or for gas,

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:16.780
then that's an attractive option

00:05:16.780 --> 00:05:19.100
for saving money and saving the planet.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:21.200
This model is already being implemented

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.740
in New York, Maryland, Colorado

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.850
and other states with incentive
programs for solar panels

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:29.300
whereby low interest
loans allow homeowners

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:31.247
to make monthly payments
that are comparable

00:05:31.247 --> 00:05:34.403
and often less than
typical electric bills.

00:05:36.806 --> 00:05:38.090
I think to date we've raised

00:05:38.090 --> 00:05:39.920
around $100 million dollars.

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.040
We have been really fortunate to have

00:05:42.040 --> 00:05:44.570
some world-class investors.

00:05:44.570 --> 00:05:47.210
Salesforce is an investor, Goldman Sachs,

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:49.800
The American Family Life
Insurance Corporation,

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:53.140
but there's $4 trillion of projects to do.

00:05:53.140 --> 00:05:55.830
I mean, there's $4 trillion worth

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.903
of buildings to
decarbonize across America.

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.600
I think the most important
thing that we're doing

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.720
is recently we were selected by the city

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:08.440
of Ithaca to decarbonize the entire city,

00:06:08.440 --> 00:06:11.220
meaning every building, no fossil fuels.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:12.870
We have an eight year timeline

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.430
by which we have to
decarbonize the entire city.

00:06:15.430 --> 00:06:17.340
So it's the first city in America,

00:06:17.340 --> 00:06:21.290
in the first city in the
world to fully decarbonize.

00:06:21.290 --> 00:06:23.240
We know that we have eight

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:25.543
or nine years to make
massive interventions

00:06:25.543 --> 00:06:27.560
in the way that we operate

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:29.080
and the way that our economy works

00:06:29.080 --> 00:06:32.470
in order to avoid the worst
impacts of climate change.

00:06:32.470 --> 00:06:34.910
And if we can decarbonize all cities

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:37.590
across America then 30%

00:06:37.590 --> 00:06:40.080
of our greenhouse gas
emissions will be avoided.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.310
And that means America
will have led the world

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:46.880
away from the worst
consequences of climate change.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:48.520
And so we're feeling the pressure,

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:49.880
but we're really excited to try

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:51.330
and step up to the challenge.

